I've a problem with audio on my HP 2560p laptop (using snd_hda_intel):
the speaker no longer works.  However, I successfully get sound on a
headphone.

I've attached the output of alsa-info.  It would be great if someone
could take a look at let me know if this is a bug in the driver or
wrong settings.

Background:

I used ALSA successfully in the past to play audio with the in-built
speaker.  At some point, I used aumix (which requires OSS modules) to
turn the volume to zero.  I believe I turned the volume back up again.
I also rebooted my laptop at some point.  I don't know if it's related
to using aumix or something else, but at some point the in-built
speaker stopped working... I can still listen to audio using a
headphone.

Another observation is that my laptop has a speaker mute button.  When
I reboot my laptop, and the BIOS or grub is running, I see that the
mute button is activated.  However, pressing the button doesn't change
anything... when the Linux kernel loads, the mute button is still on,
but when ALSA starts the button changes colour: it seems to me that
ALSA thinks that mute is off while in reality it is on.

-- 
Martin Michlmayr
http://www.cyrius.com/

